# WITH A HUD-LESS IMAGE, THE INPAINTING PASS KEEPS THE PICTURE FOR THE NEXT PAIR AND LOADS THE GENERATED COLOUR ONLY WHERE IT MAY
# CHANGE IT (2026-10-12, the last exact cut of phase 3: docs\reports\fg-3\sitting-2026-10-12\BRIEF-lib4.md, part 3).
#
# WHAT AMD'S CODE DOES. With a HUD-less image attached the last pass runs one thread a pixel and loads three whole
# pictures of the display's size: the generated colour, the HUD-less picture and the presented one. It changes a pixel
# in two cases only: the inpainting weight asks for it, or the two pictures differ there (the interface). Then, as the
# dispatch's last job, AMD COPIES THE HUD-LESS PICTURE WHOLE into the image it keeps for the next pair's interpolation
# (the "previous interpolation source"): the same 63 MiB read once more and written.
# On the three-image set the pass takes 85 us and the copy 41 where the two-image set's block form takes 19 and 58
# (docs\reports\fg-3\after-sitting-2026-10-11\REPORT-cuts-leftover.md).
#
# THE CUT, for a dispatch with a HUD-less image, no debug drawing, and 16-bit float pictures (the mod's HDR shape; the
# dispatch says so to the pass by one bit of its own in the dispatch flags, which AMD's shaders only test bit by bit):
#   1. A thread loads the HUD-less pixel (it needs it for the comparison) AND STORES IT into the image kept for the
#      next pair. AMD's copy at the dispatch's end is then not scheduled: every pixel of the picture was stored (the
#      pass covers the display rounded up to eight; a 16-bit float is loaded and stored without a change of a bit).
#   2. It loads the presented pixel and the inpainting weight (one small value), and calls AMD's function, unchanged,
#      only where the weight asks for inpainting or the two pictures differ. For every other pixel AMD's function
#      loads three values and stores nothing: not calling it changes nothing, and the generated colour is not loaded.
# In every other dispatch (no HUD-less image; a debug drawing; pictures of another format, where a load and a store
# were not judged) the pass and the copy run as before.
#
# MEASURED: see docs\reports\fg-3\sitting-2026-10-12\lib4 (the price and the judge's line).
what the inpainting pass (I10), with a HUD-less image of 16-bit floats and no debug drawing, stores the HUD-less pixel for the next pair itself (AMD's whole copy at the dispatch's end is not scheduled) and calls AMD's function only for a pixel it can change
passes ffx_frameinterpolation_inpainting_pass
wave64 it edits the pass's file, which both the cs_6_2 and the cs_6_6 (wave64) variants are compiled from, and the dispatch in ffx_frameinterpolation.cpp, which runs on every device; no wave operation; not run here on a wave64 device
file framegeneration/fsr3/include/gpu/frameinterpolation/ffx_frameinterpolation_callbacks_hlsl.h
--- old
#ifdef FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_BIND_UAV_DISOCCLUSION_MASK
--- new
// (the mod's cut fi-inpainting-keeps-the-source) the image kept for the next pair's interpolation, written by the inpainting pass
#ifdef FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_BIND_UAV_PREVIOUS_INTERPOLATION_SOURCE
    RWTexture2D<FfxFloat32x4> rw_previous_interpolation_source FFX_DECLARE_UAV(FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_BIND_UAV_PREVIOUS_INTERPOLATION_SOURCE);
#endif

#ifdef FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_BIND_UAV_DISOCCLUSION_MASK
